{start_of_chorus}
[Am]Joshua fit the battle of [E]Jericho,
[Am]Jericho, [E]Jericho,
[Am]Joshua fit the battle of [E]Jericho,
And the [E]walls came tumbling [Am]down.
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
You may [Am]talk about your king of Gideon,
You may talk about your [E]man of Saul,
There's [Am]none like good old Joshua
At the [E]battle of Jeri[Am]cho.
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
[Am]Up to the walls of Jericho
He marched with spear in [E]hand;
"Go [Am]blow those ram horns," Joshua cried,
"'Cause the [E]battle am in my [Am]hand."
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}
{x_end: Am}
